      "text": "The parametric equations give us the coordinates on the parametric curve as $x = 2 \\sin t$ and $y = 2 \\cos t.$ We can find the length of the curve by using the formula\n\\[L = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{\\left( \\frac{dx}{dt} \\right)^2 + \\left( \\frac{dy}{dt} \\right)^2} \\, dt.\\]We have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= 2 \\cos t, \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= -2 \\sin t.\n\\end{align*}So, the length of the curve is\n\\[L = \\int_0^\\pi \\sqrt{(2 \\cos t)^2 + (-2 \\sin t)^2} \\, dt = \\int_0^\\pi \\sqrt{4 \\cos^2 t + 4 \\sin^2 t} \\, dt = \\int_0^\\pi \\sqrt{4} \\, dt = \\boxed{2\\pi}.\\]. The answer is: 2\\pi",
